            <ArticleTitle>A man with saphenous vein graft aneurysms after bypass surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1815-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Saphenous vein graft (SVG) aneurysms are a rare complication of coronary artery bypass graft surgery. Patients in whom these aneurysms form a fistula with either a cardiac chamber or mediastinal vessel are even more uncommon and present a difficult diagnostic and therapeutic challenge. We present a patient with SVG aneurysms and a fistula to the left atrium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
